(pointed to the location of a large commercial and manufacturing) Tj T*
(metropolis as it did to the shores of Commencement bay when the) Tj T*
(Northern Pacific located here the terminus of its main line on Puget) Tj T*
(sound. In its history, years have witnessed more life and growth, more) Tj T*
(progress in business and wealth and the creation of more permanent) Tj T*
(values of property, than decades in the history of older and admittedly) Tj T*
(prosperous cities of the eastern states. Eight years ago, at the) Tj T*
(beginning of the present decade, Tacoma had a population of but) Tj T*
(seven hundred and twenty souls, its streets were ungraded and full) Tj T*
(of stumps, and its business blocks were few and of but the cheapest) Tj T*
(of frame structures. What mighty things have been wrought in the) Tj T*
(brief time which has since elapsed! Now it has many miles of graded) Tj T*
(streets, of water and gas mains, of telegraph, telephone and electric) Tj T*
(light wires and street railways, solid blocks of brick and stone) Tj T*
(business structures, large and commodious opera house, public schools,) Tj T*
(seminaries and academies, elegant hotels, large factories, great and) Tj T*
(expanding docks, warehouses and shipping facilities, a taxable property) Tj T*
(of $6,555,400 and a population of twenty thousand souls. It is this) Tj T*
(Tacoma of to-day, bustling, vigorous, full of life and business, and) Tj T*
(advancing with prodigious strides, which is treated of in the following) Tj T*
(pages of engravings and descriptive matter. These engravings, elegant) Tj T*
(and artistic as they are, fall far short of doing justice to a city) Tj T*
(whose prosperity, vitality and progressiveness it is impossible to) Tj T*
(convey to paper. They are the Tacoma of to-day, but will be almost as) Tj T*
(unlike the great city ten years from now which will bear that name, as) Tj T*
(they are unlike that city of board shanties which occupied this site) Tj T*
(eight years ago.) Tj T*
