(GRAIN SHIPMENTS AND FLOURING MILLS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Less than a year has passed since Tacoma entered regularly into the) Tj T*
(shipping of grain and flour to foreign markets, though practically this) Tj T*
(business began the present year, after the completion of the tunnel) Tj T*
(through the mountains. During the year ending June 30, 1888, there) Tj T*
(were shipped from this port eight hundred and thirty-eight thousand) Tj T*
(two hundred and thirty-three bushels of grain, and the estimated) Tj T*
(quantity for the current fiscal year is four million five hundred) Tj T*
(thousand bushels, requiring a grain fleet of sixty vessels, being an) Tj T*
(average of one cargo dispatched every six days. Owing to the fact that) Tj T*
(vessels can enter Puget sound more cheaply than the Columbia river,) Tj T*
(and can discharge and receive cargo and get to sea again cheaper,) Tj T*
(charters are much lower here than at Portland, and the price of wheat) Tj T*
(proportionately higher. For this reason the wheat along the line of) Tj T*
(the Northern Pacific, which, before the completion of the road over) Tj T*
(the mountains, was shipped to Portland, now comes to Tacoma. As the) Tj T*
(Northern Pacific and its branches and connecting lines ramify the) Tj T*
(entire wheat region east of the Cascades, where twenty million bushels) Tj T*
(will be produced this year, it can be seen that an estimate of four) Tj T*
(million five hundred thousand bushels for the present year is not a) Tj T*
(large one. Wheat warehouses, with a capacity of five hundred thousand) Tj T*
(bushels, have been built on the water front, and are being doubled) Tj T*
(in size. The Northern Pacific Elevator Co. is erecting a four-story) Tj T*
(elevator, with a capacity of a million bushels, and has elevators and) Tj T*
(warehouses at all the principal shipping points in the interior. The) Tj T*
(only steam flouring mill on Puget sound is located here. Not only is) Tj T*
(this port superior to Portland as a general shipping point for grain) Tj T*
(and flour, but it has special advantages in the China trade, which) Tj T*
(consumes twenty-five hundred barrels per month of Pacific coast flour.) Tj T*
(Recognizing this, gentlemen engaged largely in manufacturing flour) Tj T*
(in Oregon are erecting an immense mill with a daily capacity of one) Tj T*
(thousand barrels, which will begin grinding next season.) Tj T*
