(COAL AND IRON RESOURCES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Coal shipments from the port of Tacoma average twenty-seven thousand) Tj T*
(tons a month, being the product of mines situated in the region) Tj T*
(immediately tributary to the city and along the line of the Northern) Tj T*
(Pacific. These mines are owned and operated by the Carbon Hill Coal) Tj T*
(Co., the Wilkeson Coal and Coke Co., the Tacoma Coal Co., the South) Tj T*
(Prairie Coal Co., all in the Puyallup region, and the Bucoda Coal Co.,) Tj T*
(south of the city. Nearly all these shipments go by sail and steamer) Tj T*
(to the San Francisco market. The Durham coal mines, sixty miles east) Tj T*
(of Tacoma, are just being opened, and provision is being made for a) Tj T*
(daily output of three hundred tons. This is fine coking coal, and will) Tj T*
(be used by the great iron smelters to be erected at Cle Elum. The mine) Tj T*
(is the property of the Pacific Investment Co. At Roslyn, on the east) Tj T*
(side of the mountains, are the mines of the Northern Pacific Coal Co.,) Tj T*
(whose headquarters are in this city. Inexhaustible in quantity, and) Tj T*
(much of it making the finest quality of coke, the coal deposits about) Tj T*
(Tacoma must build up a very large city here. Iron ore of a superior) Tj T*
(quality lies in immense and easily accessible deposits almost at the) Tj T*
(city?s gate. Coal, coke and iron, with limestone in abundance, suggest) Tj T*
(the great manufacturing possibilities, to take advantage of which an) Tj T*
(immense enterprise is already on foot, in the form of a gigantic iron) Tj T*
(smelting plant, to be erected at Cle Elum, near the Roslyn mines, by) Tj T*
(the Moss Bay Iron Co., one of the largest institutions of its kind in) Tj T*
(England, and the huge reduction works soon to be erected at Tacoma by a) Tj T*
(company recently organized for that purpose.) Tj T*
