(GENERAL OFFICES OF THE NORTHERN PACIFIC RAILROAD.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At the edge of the bluff overlooking the harbor, and at the head of the) Tj T*
(grade leading down to the water front, stands the elegant, commodious) Tj T*
(building used for the general offices of the Northern Pacific. It is a) Tj T*
(most substantial structure of brick and iron, cemented on the exterior) Tj T*
(walls, having a basement, three stories and an attic, with asbestos) Tj T*
(felt under each floor, and was completed in the fall of 1888 at a total) Tj T*
(cost of $125,000.00. In all, the building contains fifty-three office) Tj T*
(and store rooms, and nineteen commodious fire-proof vaults, one being) Tj T*
(connected with every suite of rooms. It is heated by hot water, and) Tj T*
(the interior finishing and furnishing is very elegant and ornamental.) Tj T*
(In addition to the offices of the Northern Pacific, the building will) Tj T*
(be occupied by the western office of the land department of the N.) Tj T*
(P. R. R., managed by Mr. Paul Schulze, the Tacoma Land Company, Mr.) Tj T*
(Isaac W. Anderson, manager, the Northern Pacific Coal Company, and the) Tj T*
(Northern Pacific Express Company. This elegant and imposing structure,) Tj T*
(occupying such a commanding site, will always be one of the most) Tj T*
(striking architectural features of the city, proclaiming to the world) Tj T*
(the confidence the officers of the Northern Pacific have in the future) Tj T*
(of the great city springing up at its western terminus.) Tj T*
