(for the excellent public school system they have created as for the) Tj T*
(wonders they have achieved in the construction of a substantial city) Tj T*
(in so brief a period. Public schools have been recognized as one of) Tj T*
(the fundamental necessities of society throughout the west generally,) Tj T*
(and wherever the nucleus of a city has been planted, the public school) Tj T*
(system has formed part of the seed. Especially in Tacoma is this regard) Tj T*
(for the educational welfare of the rising generation exhibited in a) Tj T*
(marked degree. Six school buildings have been erected, engravings of) Tj T*
(which are given on the opposite page, and these will soon be inadequate) Tj T*
(to accommodate the children applying for admission. In 1880 but one) Tj T*
(hundred children attended the single school. By 1884 this had increased) Tj T*
(to four hundred, to five hundred in 1885, and now, in 1888, no less) Tj T*
(than fifteen hundred children are enjoying the advantages of free) Tj T*
(instruction in the six school buildings. The schools are thoroughly) Tj T*
(systematized and graded from the primary to the high school department,) Tj T*
(and are under the charge of a competent superintendent, ably assisted) Tj T*
(by a large corps of teachers. The enterprise, liberality and good) Tj T*
(citizenship displayed in thus providing promptly and adequately for the) Tj T*
(needs of the ever-increasing numbers of school children, is an evidence) Tj T*
(of the energy and intelligence of the citizens, and explains much that) Tj T*
(seems wonderful in the phenomenal growth of the city.) Tj T*
