(to buy lots at $50 and $100 that will in a few years be worth ten) Tj T*
(times their present value. Property in residence sections is a safe) Tj T*
(investment. The Sawyer addition lies near the center of the residence) Tj T*
(portion and contains one hundred and ninety lots, sixty-five of which) Tj T*
(are sold. Water is on the ground and street cars are within two) Tj T*
(blocks, while the Methodist university will be erected within one) Tj T*
(block. Oakland addition lies in the southwestern portion of the city) Tj T*
(overlooking the natural park, and is most desirable residence property.) Tj T*
(Traver?s addition is but one-half mile from the city limits, easy of) Tj T*
(access by good roads, and near the present terminus of the steam motor) Tj T*
(line. This is most desirable property, and is selling at $100 per lot) Tj T*
(on easy terms. White & Ouimette?s addition lies one and one-half miles) Tj T*
(from the limits, near the line of Hart?s railroad, and lots are sold at) Tj T*
($50 each on the installment plan. Five years from now those who fail) Tj T*
(to invest in this class of residence property will be regretting it as) Tj T*
(keenly as do those now who made the same mistake about $50 and $100) Tj T*
(lots five years ago. The increase in real estate values is best shown) Tj T*
(by the city assessment roll. In 1880 it was but $517,927; in 1886,) Tj T*
