(Between the harbor of Tacoma as it was in 1880 and as it is to-day) Tj T*
(there is as strong a contrast as between a wilderness and a walled) Tj T*
(city, and yet the harbor of the city of ten years hence will present) Tj T*
(a still stronger contrast. Along the western shore of Commencement) Tj T*
(bay run the numerous tracks of the Northern Pacific, along which have) Tj T*
(been erected most costly wharfs, warehouses, docks, coal bunkers and) Tj T*
(numerous other commercial facilities. Saw mills have multiplied and) Tj T*
(other factories are being located. On the opposite page is given an) Tj T*
(engraving of a portion of the water front, showing coal bunkers, saw) Tj T*
(mill and other features. Between the row of piles on the right of) Tj T*
(the foreground and the city, which lies to the left, is the channel) Tj T*
(of Puyallup river, not accessible to vessels at low tide. Here most) Tj T*
(extensive improvements have been planned, consisting of dredging the) Tj T*
(channel and constructing deep water docks along both sides of it. An) Tj T*
(immense area of mud flats lies back of the row of piling mentioned,) Tj T*
(which will be cut off from water by this work, and rendered available) Tj T*
(for commercial purposes. Here will be located factories, warehouses) Tj T*
(and wholesale stores of the future city. A mammoth saw mill is already) Tj T*
(being constructed on the flats. By this means large additions will be) Tj T*
(made to the water front, already six miles in length, and the docks) Tj T*
(and channel will pierce the heart of the city. Objection has sometimes) Tj T*
