(SCENERY OF PUGET SOUND.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(From a picturesque standpoint, Puget sound possesses attractions of a) Tj T*
(high order. Its shores, which, in the main, come down in bluffy steeps) Tj T*
(to the very margin of the waters, are lined with verdant firs. Here and) Tj T*
(there the rolling hills are broken, where some stream pours down from) Tj T*
(the mountains and flows through a fertile valley, covered with a rank) Tj T*
(growth of forests of cedar, fir, maple, alder, cottonwood and creeping) Tj T*
(vines, save where the hand of man has cleared a way for the plow, and) Tj T*
(converted the forest wild into green meadows and fields of grain. Back) Tj T*
(from the shores, the forests rise in successive terraces as they climb) Tj T*
(the mountain sides, and soften their rugged outlines clear to their) Tj T*
(summits, save where here and there some giant snow peak thrusts its) Tj T*
(hoary head far above the green mantle of the mountains, and challenges) Tj T*
(the traveler?s eye from whatever direction he may be approaching. On a) Tj T*
(clear, warm, bracing day in early summer time, the traveler down the) Tj T*
(sound has almost constantly in view one of these snowy summits. Mount) Tj T*
(Tacoma to the southeast, Mount Baker to the northeast, and the long,) Tj T*
(serrated ridge of the Olympic range to the west, all hold their snowy) Tj T*
(crowns aloft for his inspection. The calm, deep waters of the sound,) Tj T*
(like the bosom of a mountain tarn, reflect the sun?s rays by day, and) Tj T*
(by night glisten under the shimmering light of the moon. A journey down) Tj T*
(its winding channels, through its narrow passages, among its hundreds) Tj T*
(of islands, past its cities, towns and busy mills, the eye constantly) Tj T*
(greeted by new and ever-changing landscapes of beauty, is one never to) Tj T*
(be forgotten by him who takes it when a clear sky and full moon combine) Tj T*
(to reveal its beauties, both day and night. Tacoma?s location renders) Tj T*
(it the best headquarters for tourists while enjoying the beauties of) Tj T*
(the sound.) Tj T*
